    // Explosion scar (2026-07-23): replaces the fallout particle spray. The
    // nuke_scar texture (Zero-K scar5_big) is stretched over r 94 (~120% of
    // the slag ring + voronoi fragment overhang) at full strength, alpha
    // shaping the falloff. Deliberately FIRST band, before destroy_all: the
    // r 32 core's debris shower and the shatter ring's rigid debris (r 64,
    // fragments overhang up to ~cell_size past it) carry scorched pixels,
    // and resolidified rubble stays scarred. The stain is a solid disc
    // through the ground, so crater walls exposed later are scarred too.
    // The shatter wave is fuse-5 so this scar is on screen a beat before
    // the ground bursts (extrapolation displays 4f ahead).
    {
      "stain": {
        "r": [
          0,
          94
        ],
        "strength": 1,
        "texture": "nuke_scar"
      }
    },
    // Thermal pulse (2026-07-30; in the soot pass since 2026-08-02). Same
    // pass as the stain, same reasoning: soot and heat land together, five
    // ticks before the shatter wave, so by the time the ground bursts it is
    // already glowing — rock's 150 flip to core:hot_rock is what made this
    // band visible — and the r 64 debris is carved out of hot rock.
    //
    // The one FADED disc in the mod (falloff: 0; the default is flat). A
    // flat pulse ends in a razor 170°-beside-ambient circle, and at nuke
    // scale that edge is a visible perfect ring of glow; every smaller
    // stamp keeps the flat disc precisely because at r 4-12 the edge
    // doesn't read. The glow has to die where the SOOT dies, and the soot
    // is the scar texture's alpha, not the stain's r 94 box: measured on
    // nuke_scar.png, mean alpha crosses 50% by ~r 49 and even the
    // starburst streak tips are spent by ~r 78 — the box's outer band is
    // empty fringe. 220 puts the 150° hot_rock flip line at d 78 (deposit
    // 130 exactly), right at the last streak tips. The profile from a 20°
    // ambient: capped at 190° out to d 43 (well inside the crater, which
    // masks it), glowing 190→150 across the scar's dense body, then
    // sub-flip warmth that still lights fuels out to ~d 139 (core:wood
    // 80) and reaches true zero at 192. On a 0° ambient map the flip
    // pulls in to d 61 — the streaky outer third of the scar stays
    // glowless there.
    //
    // The 190 limit is unchanged — the "not-ground-melting" half:
    // core:sand melts at 200 and hot_rock needs 220 to run to lava, so no
    // amount of nuking liquefies ground by heat alone. The r 65 melt wave
    // still makes its slag ring — that is a transmute, not a temperature,
    // and the two do not fight: slag spawns at 200, and a POSITIVE
    // modify_temperature never cools anything already above its limit, so
    // the 255 nuke_burst fireballs raining +25/limit-150 afterwards leave
    // both the glow apron and the slag pool alone.
    {
      "modify_temperature": {
        "r": [
          0,
          192
        ],
        "amount": 220,
        "limit": 190,
        "falloff": 0
      }
    },
